    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2009-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The least common denominator of the small fractions is \\(12,\\) so multiply top and bottom by \\(12:\\) \\[ \\dfrac{\\frac13-\\frac14}{\\frac12-\\frac13}=\\dfrac{4-3}{6-4}=\\dfrac12. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply the numerator and denominator by \\(12\\)",
        "\\(\\dfrac13-\\dfrac14=\\dfrac1{12}\\) and \\(\\dfrac12-\\dfrac13=\\dfrac16\\)"
      ],
